    "id": "p16-q4-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "4",
    "prompt": "Draw a number line marked from $0$ to $6$, and then indicate on it where the markers for $\\frac{2}{3}$, $\\frac{10}{3}$, $5\\frac{1}{3}$, $\\frac{16}{9}$, $\\frac{18}{6}$ and $4\\frac{2}{6}$ are located.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "From left to right: $\\frac{2}{3}$, $\\frac{16}{9}$, $\\frac{18}{6}$, $\\frac{10}{3}$, $4\\frac{2}{6}$, $5\\frac{1}{3}$, at positions $\\frac{2}{3}$, $1\\frac{7}{9}$, $3$, $3\\frac{1}{3}$, $4\\frac{1}{3}$ and $5\\frac{1}{3}$ respectively.",
      "worked": "Mark the whole numbers from $0$ to $6$ at equal intervals. Divide each unit into nine equal subintervals; each third spans three of these subintervals.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{10}{3}&=3\\frac{1}{3}\\\\\\frac{16}{9}&=1\\frac{7}{9}\\\\\\frac{18}{6}&=3\\\\4\\frac{2}{6}&=4\\frac{1}{3}\\end{align*}$$\n\nPlace each marker at its corresponding position, retaining the original fraction or mixed numeral as its label.",
